\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces (a) Distributed vertical power delivery: $M{=}49$ regulator cells convert 48\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}V to 1\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}V beneath or behind the compute die, so the high-current rail travels micrometres. (b) The synthesised hybrid regulator, a three-to-one switched-capacitor stage feeding a three-phase buck stage, with the rail carried by each branch annotated. (c) Information flow of the framework: converter synthesis and the component library determine an explicit physical stack, which is shared by the electrical, thermal, mechanical and realizability models. The electrical and thermal models are iterated to a fixed point; the converged field is applied one-way to the mechanical model.}}{3}{figure.1}}
\newlabel{fig:system}{{1}{3}{(a) Distributed vertical power delivery: $M{=}49$ regulator cells convert 48\,V to 1\,V beneath or behind the compute die, so the high-current rail travels micrometres. (b) The synthesised hybrid regulator, a three-to-one switched-capacitor stage feeding a three-phase buck stage, with the rail carried by each branch annotated. (c) Information flow of the framework: converter synthesis and the component library determine an explicit physical stack, which is shared by the electrical, thermal, mechanical and realizability models. The electrical and thermal models are iterated to a fixed point; the converged field is applied one-way to the mechanical model}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Physical stack and power path for the two integration alternatives. (a) Embedded: the converter cells are built into the $1.30$\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}mm substrate and the through-substrate field carries the 48\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}V input rail. (b) Backside: the cells are mounted on the underside of a $0.30$\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}mm substrate and the identical field carries the 1\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}V output rail at the full cell current. Arrow width indicates segment current on a logarithmic scale. The two are electrically distinct despite sharing the same converter.}}{3}{figure.2}}
\newlabel{fig:stack}{{2}{3}{Physical stack and power path for the two integration alternatives. (a) Embedded: the converter cells are built into the $1.30$\,mm substrate and the through-substrate field carries the 48\,V input rail. (b) Backside: the cells are mounted on the underside of a $0.30$\,mm substrate and the identical field carries the 1\,V output rail at the full cell current. Arrow width indicates segment current on a logarithmic scale. The two are electrically distinct despite sharing the same converter}{figure.2}{}}
