\newlabel{tab:final}{{II}{5}{Final comparison on the frozen repartitioned pair. The corner-joint displacement driver $\du $ and the local inelastic response $\Delta \varepsilon _{\mathrm {in}}$ are separate quantities and are reported separately: $\du $ is the in-plane displacement the global solve imposes on the joint, $\Delta \varepsilon _{\mathrm {in}}$ the dimensionless per-cycle strain increment the viscoplastic submodel returns for it. Both architectures are geometrically realizable and process-conditional; neither is qualified}{table.2}{}}
